  "limitations": [
    "Local modeled failure exits are not evidence that the corresponding event is reachable at runtime.",
    "CALL ON EXCEPTION is a call-level exception clause, not a generic catch for nonzero business status from a callee.",
    "NOT ON EXCEPTION success still requires LEAF-STATUS checking; a normal return may report business failure.",
    "NOT ON SIZE ERROR is the arithmetic success alternative, not a statement that runs after a size-error handler.",
    "Cross-program contexts and local exceptional graphs do not imply full interprocedural execution semantics.",
    "All actual business scenarios are NOT_EXECUTED; no compiler or runtime has been used.",
    "Main excludes unsafe regression and unsupported-boundary source directories."
  ]
